1
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,820
It'll work out somehow.

2
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,880
Anyone without a job, come to my place.

3
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:04,480
I don't have one either, but don't worry.

4
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:11,440
Look, even the steel is burning.

5
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:18,220
It'll all work out somehow, eventually.

6
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:23,500
You understand, right?
I understand, I understand.

7
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,400
Once you understand, shut up and follow me.

8
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:43,820
Maiso, this is Kariha, deploying.

9
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:48,800
Right.

10
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:51,360
Good morning.

11
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:52,800
Morning, Ryo-chan.

12
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:56,380
Ryo-san, hold on a sec,
I'm clearing it up now.

13
00:01:56,940 --> 00:01:58,140
Aaaah!

14
00:01:58,140 --> 00:01:59,320
Senpai!

15
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:01,880
Don't go using my desk without permission.

16
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,800
S-sorry.

17
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:09,220
Ryo-chan,
why are you taking it out on everyone?

18
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:12,000
That's right,
poor Terai-san is being treated unfairly!

19
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:14,020
Shut up, shut up, shut up!

20
00:02:14,020 --> 00:02:17,480
I'm the one who's pitiful here, too!

21
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:21,080
I turned over a new leaf and
honestly bet on the favorite.

22
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:23,940
Of all things,
the jockey had to fall off the horse!

23
00:02:26,220 --> 00:02:28,500
Oh no, the chair got bent out of shape.

24
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:30,580
Oh no, I broke the fine item.

25
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,960
Show a little concern for me, too.

26
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:35,460
You brought it on yourself.

27
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:38,320
This chair's no good anymore, is it?

28
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:39,440
Hand it over!

29
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:41,500
For something like this, you just do this:

30
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:44,740
Do it like this and it'll be fixed.

31
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:47,500
Heh.

32
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,920
You can't sit like that.

33
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:51,860
That's museum material

34
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:54,300
It'll be deducted from next month's salary.

35
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:55,640
Shut up!

36
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:57,580
Do it like this and you can sit on it.

37
00:02:57,580 --> 00:02:59,520
See, it's comfortable to sit on.

38
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:00,700
Not bad.

39
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:06,460
Oh no, now the bookshelf

40
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:07,073
Damn,

41
00:03:07,123 --> 00:03:10,880
why is there a bookshelf
in a place like this?

42
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:15,880
What are we going to do about this,
Ryo-chan?

43
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:17,340
If you just do it like this
with something like this,

44
00:03:20,860 --> 00:03:22,760
The wind over here is rough too.

45
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:24,600
Just stop it already!

46
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:26,680
Rope, hold it with this and stop!

47
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:29,000
The window broke.

48
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,600
There's a hole in the roof, too.

49
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,440
Wow! It's Mezumi!

50
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:37,260
Reiko, it's me!

51
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:38,380
Ow!

52
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:39,440
Get out of the way!

53
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:51,760
What happened? What on earth is this?

54
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:54,160
Chief!

55
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:57,580
What on earth do you
two think you're doing...

56
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:01,920
Chief! That's...

57
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:03,700
What?

58
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:21,600
Who on earth did this?

59
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:27,160
It's you again, Ryotsu.

60
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:30,240
It was, you could say, an accident.

61
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:33,440
There were circumstances that led to this.

62
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:36,940
You idiot!

63
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:41,120
Of all times, why now?

64
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:42,600
At a time like this?

65
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:46,800
The day after tomorrow morning, an
inspection team is coming from headquarters.

66
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:48,220
Inspection?

67
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:48,900
Inspection?

68
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:52,660
It's a fact-finding inspection of the police box,
you idiot!

69
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:56,720
If headquarters finds out about this scandal,
you know what will happen, right?

70
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:59,080
Don't make that face, ugh.

71
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:04,020
Even if we request to change the inspection schedule now,
it probably won't work.

72
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:06,380
This is bad.

73
00:05:06,380 --> 00:05:08,720
Leave it to me, Chief!

74
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:12,820
I'll make sure the station is back
to normal by the day after tomorrow.

75
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:14,840
You'd better mean that.

76
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:17,540
Of course, Chief!

77
00:05:17,540 --> 00:05:21,720
Anyway, everyone assembles here
at 8 a.m. the day after tomorrow.

78
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:24,640
Until then,
carry on with your normal duties.

79
00:05:24,640 --> 00:05:27,560
Ryotsu, I'll decide your punishment then.

80
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:29,360
Wash your neck and await the axe.

81
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:33,420
But without a station,
how are we supposed to work?

82
00:05:33,420 --> 00:05:37,580
Let that idiot over there figure that out.

83
00:05:39,820 --> 00:05:43,060
Chief, I'll definitely get the
station fixed back to normal.

84
00:05:43,060 --> 00:05:44,240
I'll keep working too.

85
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:47,060
I'll get us through this emergency,
I promise.

86
00:05:47,060 --> 00:05:47,820
Chief.

87
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,420
No time to waste!

88
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:52,620
The day after tomorrow means
the day after tomorrow...

89
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:53,760
We're running out of time!

90
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:03,120
What, everyone gets cold, contemptuous
stares now and then, don't they?

91
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:06,200
Everyone's going to smash up some equipment when they're frustrated,
aren't they?

92
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:07,880
There's no such thing.

93
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:11,380
Well, maybe not that often.

94
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:13,180
Anyway, this is an emergency.

95
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:17,140
Sorry, but the entire Nakagawa Group
will mobilize to rush to the police box.

96
00:06:17,140 --> 00:06:19,680
Please don't count on us this time.

97
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:21,120
What?

98
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:24,740
Should we really keep
following our senior like this?

99
00:06:24,740 --> 00:06:28,540
Since we've decided to take this
opportunity to think it over carefully.

100
00:06:29,280 --> 00:06:30,320
Insolent little...

101
00:06:30,940 --> 00:06:32,140
Reiko-chan.

102
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,340
Let's see what you can do, Ryo-chan.

103
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:37,960
Terai, we've known each other a long time,
haven't we?

104
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:40,080
You talk those two into it.

105
00:06:40,940 --> 00:06:44,080
I have a family I have to protect.

106
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:46,600
Fine, do as you please.

107
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,300
I'm not asking you lot for anything anymore.

108
00:06:48,940 --> 00:06:50,780
We'll be heading back to the station.

109
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:54,500
Let me know once you've decided on a plan,
Officer Ryotsu.

110
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,000
Isn't this a wallet?

111
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:20,500
Yeah, getting this thing back to
normal by the day after tomorrow...

112
00:07:21,060 --> 00:07:23,060
There's no way that's possible, Ryo-san.

113
00:07:23,620 --> 00:07:24,680
Please, somehow!

114
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:26,620
As long as it looks back to normal for now,

115
00:07:26,620 --> 00:07:30,160
papercraft or a quick patch job,
anything's fine. Please!

116
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:32,740
That's not how it works.

117
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:35,020
If you do this for me,

118
00:07:35,020 --> 00:07:38,020
I might as well have you
renovate my dad's shop too.

119
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:39,654
Come to think of it,

120
00:07:39,704 --> 00:07:43,160
there was also talk of rebuilding it
as a big apartment building, right?

121
00:07:44,300 --> 00:07:45,640
Really, Ryo-san?

122
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:49,740
Old man Tsukudajima's also
tired of living in an apartment,

123
00:07:49,740 --> 00:07:54,640
so he's supposedly said he wants to build a house on the ground again, or so they say...
or maybe not.

124
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:58,440
Please let us take on that story.

125
00:07:58,960 --> 00:07:59,280
Well then,

126
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:02,220
we'll do our best somehow.

127
00:08:02,220 --> 00:08:03,080
Really?

128
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:06,660
When unreason prevails,
reason must give way.

129
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:09,080
Next, we have to find
a room for the parolee.

130
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:17,660
Is it true they've found
a property for the parolee?

131
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:22,400
Knowing Ryo-chan,
it's bound to be somewhere outrageous.

132
00:08:22,820 --> 00:08:26,080
Ryo-san said he went to around here,
didn't he?

133
00:08:26,740 --> 00:08:28,620
Hey, this way, over here!

134
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:32,540
It's here! Come up in the elevator.

135
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:45,700
It's huge and clean, too.

136
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:47,260
How did you get this place?

137
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:50,840
That's just a taste of my skills, you know.

138
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:53,180
Well, make yourselves at home,
don't hold back.

139
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:57,320
It feels strange that a
parolee gets such a nice place.

140
00:08:57,920 --> 00:09:00,740
Ryo-chan,
I wonder if you've done something bad.

141
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:02,360
I can hear everything you're saying!

142
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:02,980
What?

143
00:09:04,940 --> 00:09:06,160
These are hard times, after all.

144
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:10,860
I figured there'd be a property no one wanted to rent,
that the real estate agent couldn't get rid of.

145
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:13,980
I bargained them down to 3,000 yen a day.

146
00:09:13,980 --> 00:09:16,740
On the condition that I
air it out and clean it.

147
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:18,980
For a room like this, that's cheap.

148
00:09:18,980 --> 00:09:20,680
As expected of you, senpai.

149
00:09:20,680 --> 00:09:23,400
Don't praise him, Tee-chan,
or he'll get cocky again.

150
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:27,680
Wow, the toilet has a bidet!

151
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:30,100
And the bathroom mirror is huge, too.

152
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:32,400
There's even one that
blows air out with a whoosh!

153
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:33,800
It's like a department store!

154
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:37,580
Comparing it to a department store
is so typically down-to-earth of you.

155
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:42,220
Chief Ohara

156
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:45,560
How is it, Chief? Our temporary police box?

157
00:09:46,060 --> 00:09:48,100
Please, make yourself at home.

158
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:50,440
There's even a leather sofa.

159
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:53,360
I can't really take it easy, but...

160
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:55,360
There's no need to worry, Chief.

161
00:09:55,360 --> 00:10:01,180
We've also arranged the repairs for Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box,
so rest assured.

162
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:02,040
I see.

163
00:10:07,580 --> 00:10:10,740
When it counts, I get things done.

164
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:18,920
I'm sure the police box
was around here somewhere...

165
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:24,140
Notice: Police box relocated.

166
00:10:24,780 --> 00:10:27,020
Well, what the heck.

167
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:43,420
Reiko, lend me your nail clippers.
My hangnail hurts.

168
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:48,700
Hei-chan, there seems to be a
problem with the night shift duty log.

169
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:54,800
Terai-san,
are these all the ledgers you carried?

170
00:10:57,900 --> 00:11:01,460
Isn't Granny Hashizume's poetry
recitation group this weekend?

171
00:11:04,220 --> 00:11:05,140
Reiko-n!

172
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:06,180
Did you call me?

173
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,740
Granny Hashizume's...

174
00:11:08,740 --> 00:11:09,840
What?

175
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:12,360
So that's why you wanted the nail clippers?

176
00:11:13,300 --> 00:11:15,340
Argh! This is going nowhere!

177
00:11:16,020 --> 00:11:18,740
Something's off. We've been talking
past each other this whole time.

178
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:22,300
I just can't feel at ease in a
room bigger than six tatami mats.

179
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:25,380
Yeah, our work efficiency
has definitely gotten worse.

180
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:27,280
Don't be so greedy!

181
00:11:29,020 --> 00:11:33,060
Why is the exit above the beer?

182
00:11:33,060 --> 00:11:35,240
I only wanted to ask for directions.

183
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:37,260
So you climbed the stairs?

184
00:11:38,180 --> 00:11:41,280
The elevator's stopped for regular maintenance,
you know.

185
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,100
Senpai, this place really isn't

186
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:46,660
suitable for a police box, Ryo-san.

187
00:11:46,660 --> 00:11:48,600
Let's move, Ryo-chan.

188
00:11:49,040 --> 00:11:50,120
Don't say it so easily.

189
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:53,760
Do you really think a perfect property
like this would turn up so easily?

190
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:56,100
Found it!

191
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:05,360
This is it?

192
00:12:08,660 --> 00:12:10,060
W-what?!

193
00:12:11,620 --> 00:12:12,940
Damn you!

194
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:20,780
It's on the first floor
and faces the street, too.

195
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:23,320
It's also fairly close to
the original police box.

196
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:27,440
Best of all, it's a super deal where
you only have to pay the utilities.

197
00:12:27,900 --> 00:12:28,740
But, senpai...

198
00:12:28,740 --> 00:12:29,680
Ryo-san...

199
00:12:30,150 --> 00:12:34,260
But Ryo-chan,
this place isn't an izakaya, you know!

200
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:37,400
Size-wise, it's an eight-mat room, right?

201
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:42,480
Sure, the red lantern out front does
kind of look like a police light.

202
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:45,740
Kei-chan,
you're letting Ryo-chan pull you along.

203
00:12:46,310 --> 00:12:47,960
Okay, okay, there we go.

204
00:12:56,180 --> 00:12:58,880
There, doesn't it look
like the birthplace now?

205
00:12:58,880 --> 00:13:03,020
If you go and do something like that without permission,
you'll be in the way of business, Ryo-san.

206
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:04,960
Do you have permission for this?

207
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:09,800
Ryo-san?

208
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:11,980
Yo! You're as lively as ever

209
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:16,620
Ryo-san, we're about to head out now.

210
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:19,800
It's our summer vacation a little early.

211
00:13:20,620 --> 00:13:21,800
So that's the deal.

212
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:22,560
Hah.

213
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:25,580
If a police officer will
watch the station for us,

214
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:28,160
there's nothing more reassuring than that.

215
00:13:28,160 --> 00:13:31,000
Well then, we're counting on you, Ryo-san.

216
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:32,780
Bye-bye!

217
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:36,340
Have a good trip!
Don't forget the souvenirs.

218
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:40,340
If that's the case, shall we make use of it?

219
00:13:40,340 --> 00:13:41,520
Kei-chan.

220
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:43,580
It's only until the day after tomorrow,
after all.

221
00:13:43,580 --> 00:13:44,900
Even Terai-san?

222
00:13:45,540 --> 00:13:48,700
As they say, home is wherever you make it.

223
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:51,660
Aaaaaah!

224
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:53,340
Let's sneak off, then.

225
00:13:53,340 --> 00:13:54,540
Me, I'll have beer.

226
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:57,760
And me too, then shrimp shumai, miss.

227
00:13:58,460 --> 00:13:59,820
I don't know anymore.

228
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:03,640
Temporary police box?

229
00:14:04,460 --> 00:14:05,140
Uh-oh?

230
00:14:05,220 --> 00:14:08,880
Until the day after tomorrow, this is
the Kameari Kōen-mae temporary police box.

231
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:10,940
Sorry, but please go to another shop.

232
00:14:10,940 --> 00:14:13,460
Anything's fine, just beer, beer!

233
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:14,400
Bring us some beer!

234
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:16,300
We can't serve beer, you know!

235
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:20,760
Senpai, there's no way we can work at the police box here,
is there?

236
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:22,480
That's what I said!

237
00:14:22,580 --> 00:14:26,540
Crap! If we don't take down the red lantern out front,
customers will keep pouring in!

238
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,160
Yeah!

239
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:34,660
Looks delicious! Let's start with ten beers!

240
00:14:34,820 --> 00:14:36,560
This one's on you, right?

241
00:14:36,940 --> 00:14:38,440
Then I'll just have ten!

242
00:14:38,520 --> 00:14:39,680
Me, four!

243
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:40,140
Me too!

244
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:40,960
Me too!

245
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:42,700
Hey, Umezawa!

246
00:14:43,060 --> 00:14:44,000
Coming!

247
00:14:45,260 --> 00:14:46,560
What do we do, Ryo-san?

248
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:47,980
Damn it!

249
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:05,440
Sigh...

250
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:07,260
Whoa!

251
00:15:10,820 --> 00:15:13,020
The police box has moved again,
for the third time!

252
00:15:13,260 --> 00:15:14,840
He ran off again!

253
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:38,400
I'm getting kind of confused now.

254
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:43,400
This is an applied problem using
the equation I just taught you.

255
00:15:43,980 --> 00:15:45,960
I see...

256
00:15:46,420 --> 00:15:47,860
Even if it's a half-folded origami.

257
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:52,480
All of this is stuff you stole, isn't it?

258
00:15:53,100 --> 00:15:54,980
I've told you, I don't know.

259
00:15:56,300 --> 00:15:57,880
You can't run away now.

260
00:15:57,880 --> 00:16:01,040
I think it's better for
you to come clean honestly.

261
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:03,240
If I don't know, I don't know.

262
00:16:05,080 --> 00:16:07,180
You're the one who has my underwear!

263
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:15,240
Math, then English next. Hang in there.

264
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:16,220
Yes.

265
00:16:17,020 --> 00:16:19,000
You're the one who stole it, aren't you!

266
00:16:20,140 --> 00:16:21,480
Tell the truth!

267
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:24,060
You're the one who stole it, right!

268
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:26,960
I don't know, I really don't know.

269
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:30,560
It's not that you don't know!

270
00:16:30,620 --> 00:16:32,480
You liar! Pervert! Scum!

271
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:36,260
Like this, I can't concentrate at all.

272
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:39,300
At this rate,
Naine will fail her entrance exams too.

273
00:16:40,420 --> 00:16:42,980
After all,
in exchange for tutoring for free,

274
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:46,120
making us sublet a room is unreasonable,
Ryo-chan.

275
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:50,600
you said we can't afford cram
school on the fourth floor,

276
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:52,540
so I thought it was perfect.

277
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:54,840
Could you please be a
little more reasonable?

278
00:16:54,840 --> 00:16:57,460
With all this noise,
the kids won't stop crying!

279
00:16:57,460 --> 00:16:58,420
Aaaaaah!

280
00:16:58,420 --> 00:16:59,060
Eeeeeeh!

281
00:17:16,260 --> 00:17:18,420
Excuse me.

282
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:18,680
Eeeeeeeeeh!

283
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:22,580
Whoa!

284
00:17:22,580 --> 00:17:24,840
Rechecking, rechecking, rechecking.

285
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:35,180
Nnnyeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeh!

286
00:17:42,260 --> 00:17:43,100
Something?

287
00:17:43,100 --> 00:17:44,240
No, nothing.

288
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:46,740
Well, this is a problem.

289
00:17:55,940 --> 00:17:59,220
Excuse me, could you possibly
change this 1,000-yen bill for me?

290
00:17:59,220 --> 00:18:04,560
Sorry, this is technically a police box,
so we don't do currency exchange.

291
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:06,220
Right, figures.

292
00:18:07,300 --> 00:18:08,300
Well, that's a relief.

293
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:10,260
Please wait a moment.

294
00:18:11,420 --> 00:18:13,500
Everyone, hand over whatever coins you have.

295
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:17,100
I pay for everything with cards, so...

296
00:18:17,540 --> 00:18:19,700
I don't carry coins either.

297
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:21,380
What about Terai?

298
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:25,280
I've got 238 yen.

299
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:27,040
That's nowhere near enough.

300
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:28,980
Just borrowing a bit.

301
00:18:30,100 --> 00:18:33,540
Nakagawa, go exchange this at
the convenience store up ahead.

302
00:18:35,180 --> 00:18:36,360
Is it really necessary to go this far?

303
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:37,080
Yes, it is!

304
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,680
To stay here as long as we possibly can,

305
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:42,240
we need to be friendly with
the laundromat customers too.

306
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:43,680
Please wait a moment.

307
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:45,600
Hey, sir.

308
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:48,400
If you stuff that much laundry in there,
it'll be too full.

309
00:18:49,340 --> 00:18:52,180
That's not police duty, Ryo-san.

310
00:19:10,580 --> 00:19:14,120
We're only trying to protect
the citizens' daily lives, and yet

311
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:17,280
why do we have to go through this?

312
00:19:17,280 --> 00:19:20,400
Isn't that because Ryo-chan
went and broke the police box?

313
00:19:21,180 --> 00:19:23,900
It has to be somewhere here in Kameari.

314
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:28,060
A temporary police box where we
can work in peace and without worry

315
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:32,320
Here it is.

316
00:19:32,860 --> 00:19:34,640
Here, no one will bother us,

317
00:19:35,180 --> 00:19:37,440
and we can set up a temporary police
box that won't get in anyone's way.

318
00:19:37,440 --> 00:19:39,140
It's not just any alley.

319
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:41,660
What if it starts raining?

320
00:19:41,660 --> 00:19:44,880
We can't work in a place like this, Ryo-san.

321
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:46,820
Leave it to me.

322
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:55,960
It's like an eel's bed, this police box.

323
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:59,980
With this little space, we can fit
a chair, but a desk is impossible.

324
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:03,500
This one will be the desk.

325
00:20:05,740 --> 00:20:07,540
That's how we write the paperwork.

326
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:11,280
I see.

327
00:20:12,160 --> 00:20:16,220
With this narrow space,
we can't get through unless it's one-way.

328
00:20:16,680 --> 00:20:18,200
That's already been taken care of.

329
00:20:20,280 --> 00:20:23,640
This way, there's no problem even when
we need to dispatch in an emergency.

330
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:26,040
Only Ryo-chan could pull
off something like that.

331
00:20:26,820 --> 00:20:28,900
The third floor of the building
next door is a soba shop,

332
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:31,480
and over here we have a beef
bowl place and a bento shop too,

333
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:32,780
so delivery is fast as well.

334
00:20:33,320 --> 00:20:36,020
Well, I won't make you two suffer.

335
00:20:36,920 --> 00:20:40,920
Somehow, I'm starting to feel this is the
best place of all the ones we've seen so far.

336
00:20:41,340 --> 00:20:43,560
Yes, home is where you make it, I suppose.

337
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:47,420
Above all, it looks like a place where we
can relax without worrying about anyone.

338
00:20:47,820 --> 00:20:48,540
Let's decide.

339
00:20:49,500 --> 00:20:53,420
Then this shall be our temporary
Kameari Park-mae Police Box!

340
00:20:57,680 --> 00:20:59,060
Get down! Move, move!

341
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:00,840
What is it?

342
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:01,320
What is it?

343
00:21:02,780 --> 00:21:03,360
Aaaaah!

344
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:13,160
Aaaaah! What on earth is going on? Right, this alley is
a shortcut to the station, you know, mass-producing it!

345
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:16,700
The morning commute rush.

346
00:21:18,140 --> 00:21:21,500
Our police box is...

347
00:21:28,380 --> 00:21:29,620
The police box is ready?

348
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:31,440
It's really done!

349
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:38,680
We did it!

350
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:40,060
It's our police box!

351
00:21:40,700 --> 00:21:42,660
It's a police box, Reiko-san.

352
00:21:43,180 --> 00:21:45,400
Yes, it's not an illusion, is it?

353
00:21:46,060 --> 00:21:48,360
We've finally made it back, haven't we?

354
00:21:49,060 --> 00:21:50,940
It's our police box!

355
00:21:51,980 --> 00:21:54,000
Then, please sign the handover papers.

356
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:57,080
You did well.

357
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:02,300
Then, please take care of the
matter with your family home.

358
00:22:10,900 --> 00:22:13,260
We've been waiting for you, Chief.

359
00:22:13,840 --> 00:22:15,680
Did you use magic or something?

360
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:17,920
Anyway, I'm glad we made it in time.

361
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:21,980
Got it. This is Yamashita-san from the
General Affairs Department at headquarters.

362
00:22:23,820 --> 00:22:30,660
Then, we'll begin the inspection of the police box right away.
Please, come in, come in.

363
00:22:36,960 --> 00:22:38,100
Found it!

364
00:22:38,100 --> 00:22:44,840
What's that?

365
00:22:45,420 --> 00:22:46,420
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

366
00:22:47,100 --> 00:22:49,080
The f-floor gave way!

367
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:50,440
Whoaaa!

368
00:22:51,100 --> 00:22:52,220
Ryo-chan!

369
00:22:55,940 --> 00:22:57,940
Whoaaa!

370
00:22:57,940 --> 00:22:59,220
Hehehe.

371
00:22:59,220 --> 00:23:01,480
Whoaaa!

372
00:23:02,100 --> 00:23:04,560
Whoaaa, it broke again!

373
00:23:04,560 --> 00:23:05,660
Nooo!

374
00:23:17,660 --> 00:23:18,920
What is this supposed to be?

375
00:23:18,920 --> 00:23:24,200
Here's the papercraft you ordered.
I stayed up all night to finish it.

376
00:23:24,200 --> 00:23:31,480
As long as it looks the way it did before, I don't care if it's papercraft or a painted backdrop.
Just get it done.

377
00:23:32,520 --> 00:23:34,420
Papercraft?

378
00:23:35,660 --> 00:23:37,360
What on earth is going on here?

379
00:23:37,740 --> 00:23:39,380
Could you explain?

380
00:23:40,120 --> 00:23:44,540
There's no way anyone can rebuild
a real police box in two days!

381
00:23:44,760 --> 00:23:45,200
Wait!

382
00:23:45,340 --> 00:23:45,740
Hey!

383
00:23:48,240 --> 00:23:49,200
W-what a mess!

384
00:23:49,980 --> 00:23:51,220
Kyottsu!

385
00:23:52,140 --> 00:23:53,700
You wretch!

386
00:23:56,880 --> 00:23:58,940
Y-you fool!

387
00:24:05,800 --> 00:24:06,680
Yes, welcome!

388
00:24:07,520 --> 00:24:09,320
Yes, welcome!

389
00:24:09,860 --> 00:24:11,440
Yes, welcome. Please, come in.

390
00:24:12,340 --> 00:24:14,100
Yes, welcome!

391
00:24:14,660 --> 00:24:16,280
Yes, welcome. Please.

392
00:24:17,120 --> 00:24:18,780
Yes, welcome!

393
00:24:19,360 --> 00:24:20,980
Yes, welcome.

394
00:24:21,780 --> 00:24:23,920
Um, and, and and, hey.

395
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:25,240
Excuse me, is it all right?

396
00:24:25,240 --> 00:24:26,340
Yes, welcome.

397
00:24:26,340 --> 00:24:27,820
Well then, how about a roll, a kappa roll?

398
00:24:27,820 --> 00:24:29,600
Salad roll, anything roll, roll.

399
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:30,540
What should I do, I wonder?

400
00:24:30,940 --> 00:24:33,520
Right, California rolls.

401
00:24:33,520 --> 00:24:34,280
Will you have that?

402
00:24:34,320 --> 00:24:34,660
Yeah.

403
00:24:34,660 --> 00:24:36,300
We don't have California rolls.

404
00:24:37,020 --> 00:24:39,000
This isn't America, you know.

405
00:24:39,500 --> 00:24:40,520
Sorry, no can do.

406
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:44,500
Uh, excuse me.

407
00:24:45,340 --> 00:24:46,220
Coming right up.

408
00:24:47,340 --> 00:24:49,840
Then, kushiage, kakiage, and katsuage.

409
00:24:49,840 --> 00:24:51,680
Wait, everything here is fried, right?

410
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:53,660
What do you recommend?

411
00:24:54,740 --> 00:24:56,960
Just watch out for the katsuage.

412
00:24:58,140 --> 00:25:00,720
Are they relatives?

413
00:25:00,880 --> 00:25:02,400
Yes, sorry, no can do.

414
00:25:13,680 --> 00:25:15,926
Yes, yes, welcome,

415
00:25:15,976 --> 00:25:17,920
Welcome, come right in.

416
00:25:17,920 --> 00:25:20,415
Yes, yes, welcome,

417
00:25:20,465 --> 00:25:22,620
Welcome, come right in.

418
00:25:23,280 --> 00:25:27,100
Yes, yes, welcome, welcome!

419
00:25:29,960 --> 00:25:33,820
Chief Ohara forced me
into a matchmaking meeting,

420
00:25:33,820 --> 00:25:38,020
and I figured no decent woman would show up,
but guess what, I was surprised.

421
00:25:38,020 --> 00:25:40,300
She's beautiful, kind, and can do anything.

422
00:25:40,300 --> 00:25:43,420
And she seems to have taken a liking to me!

423
00:25:43,920 --> 00:25:46,660
Next time: Ryo-san Declares His Love!

424
00:25:46,660 --> 00:25:47,780
Nice to meet you.

425
00:25:56,120 --> 00:25:56,520
Thank you.

